/-!
# Simultaneous coordinates for the original inner four-group

Lift a distinguished involution and a second generator to actual involutions
in SL₃. Their projective commutation lifts to matrix commutation, since the
scalar kernel has odd order. After putting the distinguished involution in
standard form, diagonalize the second inside its GL₂ centralizer. The
existing determinant-corrected block embedding supplies an SL₃ conjugator.
The diagonal involutions are precisely the three sign matrices, and the
original order-four subgroup is generated by the selected pair.

The resulting coordinates discharge that input of the literal odd-torus
construction. Only the independent diagonal centralizer control remains in
the exported mixing application.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
E.1.2 and E.1.5, printed pp.209--210, and E.1.14(7), printed p.214,
via Aschbacher (1982), Lemma 4.11.
-/

public section

